# Whether two intervals of the round-up interval have no member in common (IEEE 1788 disjoint): an
# operand empty, or one above the other; the default interval_rel_disjoint_1 on the meanings. Exact,
# in every rounding mode (docs/developer/design/upward.md, "Predicates and comparisons"). Requires
# the rounding mode upward set by kairn::upward::Scope and the options of docs/concepts/upward.md
# (GCC and Clang -frounding-math, MSVC /fp:strict).
kernel:        upward_rel_disjoint_1
rounding:      upward
input:         pair stored x = xu xn
input:         pair stored y = yu yn
output:        mask m
requires:      upward xu xn
requires:      upward yu yn
ensures:       certain m disjoint x y x=xu,xn y=yu,yn exact
min_precision: 1
source:        the lanes compared with the negated lanes, and a test of emptiness (the listing of the round-up interval)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        proved
domain:        extended
ieee_only:     yes
ieee_status:   proved
ieee_theorem:  proofs/theories/IeeeUpwardPredicates.v upward_rel_disjoint_1_correct
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   the result is a mask, which has no non-finite value, and a comparison with NaN is false; certain states what comes out for every canonical operand

ee = unord(xu, yu)
nx = neg(xn)
ny = neg(yn)
da = lt(xu, ny)
db = lt(yu, nx)
dd = or(da, db)
m = or(ee, dd)
